      }
    },
    {
      "key": "9a83d081-c4b8-414b-a81b-16b46979d64d",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 11, Level 4 to complete the End of Lesson Survey.",
        "name": "End of Lesson Survey",
        "progression_name": "End of Lesson Survey"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "9a83d081-c4b8-414b-a81b-16b46979d64d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "df3aad42-f6b4-4cb5-bfbe-8dbfd44994a9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4649e116-8c3f-443e-96d1-ef9d0a223d92",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students see firsthand how layouts change across screen sizes and start noticing breakpoints and issues."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4649e116-8c3f-443e-96d1-ef9d0a223d92",
        "lesson_activity.key": "83359e3c-3be4-47bf-8196-acf6ee22c50d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "bea9d973-f455-45e4-8ec8-0f73b859c975",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Today, we're going to become 'Resize Detectives' to explore how websites adapt to different screen sizes.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "bea9d973-f455-45e4-8ec8-0f73b859c975",
        "lesson_activity.key": "83359e3c-3be4-47bf-8196-acf6ee22c50d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "65af4ead-88aa-4a06-9a4e-4319f2792f73",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-video-camera\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Video:** Show students the video of website resizing. After watching the video, ask:\n- What changes?\n- What breaks?",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If possible, open a sample website and do a live demo of shrinking the browser window from desktop width down to tablet and then phone width. Ask students, \"How should layouts adapt across devices?\""
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "65af4ead-88aa-4a06-9a4e-4319f2792f73",
        "lesson_activity.key": "83359e3c-3be4-47bf-8196-acf6ee22c50d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "102c46fc-5e7f-4383-98c1-6e9ebae2b8a7",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "102c46fc-5e7f-4383-98c1-6e9ebae2b8a7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "83359e3c-3be4-47bf-8196-acf6ee22c50d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "95d42811-5698-4c7d-9e45-66331f3c0c89",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define responsiveness.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "95d42811-5698-4c7d-9e45-66331f3c0c89",
        "lesson_activity.key": "83359e3c-3be4-47bf-8196-acf6ee22c50d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "70794d80-1e92-4dcd-b047-357bd0a784bb",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students test and refine their AI-generated layouts for responsiveness across devices, using checklists and peer review to spot and fix issues.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Read the key stats aloud to students. Then, read what to consider when creating a responsive, user friendly website.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *If AI learns from old, non-responsive websites, how might that affect the layouts it creates today?*\n- *How could human designers help guide AI to create more mobile-friendly or flexible layouts?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should think critically about how the data used to train AI can shape the designs it produces. Training a model on older, non-responsive websites could lead AI to create layouts that don't work well on mobile devices. Students should consider how designers can guide or correct AI to make layouts that adapt better to different screen sizes. Some suggestions include: training AI with examples of mobile-friendly websites, using prompts that mention flexible grids or mobile usability, and defining constraints (like minimum button size or readable text) that AI must follow when generating layouts.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Software Test Engineer role, also referred to as Quality Assurance (QA) Tester.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-video-camera\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Video:** Show the \"A Day in the Life of a Software Test Engineer at GM\" video."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "70794d80-1e92-4dcd-b047-357bd0a784bb",
        "lesson_activity.key": "7eedf73d-9e9b-433e-9f64-1f65402ef874"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "6fb79027-c2ee-4b07-82a2-47e4ff04813f",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Today, you'll get to practice thinking like a Test Engineer. You'll look at an AI-generated webpage, test it for responsiveness, and then use what you find to guide the AI toward better, more responsive design choices.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6fb79027-c2ee-4b07-82a2-47e4ff04813f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "7eedf73d-9e9b-433e-9f64-1f65402ef874"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a524621d-3385-4da4-94fe-441c6855a1ee",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each student a copy of the Designing for Responsiveness activity guide.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to complete Levels 1 through 3. Explain that they will be testing and refining their AI-generated web apps from Lesson 11. If they don't have their webpage from the previous class, instruct them to copy and paste the HTML and CSS files from the exemplar in the instructions. Students open their webpages, resize the browser to simulate different device widths, and log any responsiveness issues using the checklist. They then refine prompts to fix those issues, save versions to track progress, and swap with a partner for peer feedback.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** As students test and refine, ask them to explain the issues they noticed and how their fixes improve usability across screen sizes. When observing peer review, prompt students to connect their suggestions to common responsive design patterns.",
        "progression_name": "Web App Responsiveness"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a524621d-3385-4da4-94fe-441c6855a1ee",
        "lesson_activity.key": "7eedf73d-9e9b-433e-9f64-1f65402ef874"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f358733f-d990-4b0c-aa1d-0f92296908d0",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Vocab: Responsiveness",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If students get stuck, remind them to focus on small, specific fixes (e.g., navigation collapsing, text wrapping, images resizing) rather than trying to solve everything at once."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f358733f-d990-4b0c-aa1d-0f92296908d0",
        "lesson_activity.key": "7eedf73d-9e9b-433e-9f64-1f65402ef874"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5abc96a9-3f7c-4f97-891e-811a622c21a0",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5abc96a9-3f7c-4f97-891e-811a622c21a0",
        "lesson_activity.key": "7eedf73d-9e9b-433e-9f64-1f65402ef874"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "cd2860bd-5bbf-4aa4-84ec-8e21d62e8df7",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Why should we design websites that work well on all devices and screen sizes?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should recognize that responsive design is more inclusive for all users. Push students to think about who is excluded when websites are not designed responsively, e.g. a website that only displays content well for desktops.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to complete Level 4.",
        "progression_name": "Check for Understanding",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Encourage students to reflect on their understanding of responsiveness issues by explaining what fixes they found most effective when redesigning their webpage."
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "This prompt can serve as a formative assessment. Collect student responses to gauge their understanding of responsiveness in design."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "cd2860bd-5bbf-4aa4-84ec-8e21d62e8df7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "7eedf73d-9e9b-433e-9f64-1f65402ef874"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "6b58d196-26ca-41b5-9db4-4e53d525d17b",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Key Vocabulary."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6b58d196-26ca-41b5-9db4-4e53d525d17b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "c1cb7c80-5bab-4646-8cbd-42f3d3ffe367"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "53c31329-df07-45e1-aeaf-8e0412f4de4d",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 12, Level 5 to complete the End of Lesson Survey.",
        "name": "End of Lesson Survey",
        "progression_name": "End of Lesson Survey"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "53c31329-df07-45e1-aeaf-8e0412f4de4d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "c1cb7c80-5bab-4646-8cbd-42f3d3ffe367"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8566b628-7017-4360-8664-401f2049ed84",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *If you could create a magazine about anything, what would it be? Who would read it?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students connect personal interests to an audience or community, priming them to think about purpose and audience in their digital magazine project.",
        "duration": "5",
        "name": "Warm Up"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8566b628-7017-4360-8664-401f2049ed84",
        "lesson_activity.key": "624a9385-01b9-40e0-8734-e85891423e60"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "afa61bea-9da2-49b4-89cd-e58b029b72fb",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each student a copy of the Digital Magazine Project Planning Guide.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the first part of the project requirements.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to read the rubric on the last two pages of the project planning guide.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What do you notice about the project requirements and rubric? What does success look like for this project?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students share what they notice about the project requirements and rubric and identify the components to implement in their program.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the milestone structure of the project. Explain that the Digital Magazine Project is divided into four milestones, each with its own goals and deliverables. Use the visual roadmap to preview the journey students will take — from defining their magazine concept to showcasing their final product.",
        "duration": "35",
        "name": "Activity",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students that milestones help them manage time and track progress, just like in real design and development projects. Encourage them to think of each milestone as a \"checkpoint\" to reflect on what's working, what needs improvement, and how their design aligns with their user and purpose."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "afa61bea-9da2-49b4-89cd-e58b029b72fb",
        "lesson_activity.key": "624a9385-01b9-40e0-8734-e85891423e60"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "6da8fbae-02d9-42f6-9f42-44b0945e501b",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6da8fbae-02d9-42f6-9f42-44b0945e501b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "624a9385-01b9-40e0-8734-e85891423e60"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "66504a00-62bf-4b4f-85d5-95bc79d2ca71",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain that today's focus is Milestone 1: Define Your Magazine, where students plan their magazine's concept, audience, and design direction. Direct students to open their Digital Magazine Project Guide and locate the Milestone 1 section. Have them read through the Goals and Deliverables so they understand what needs to be completed by the end of this milestone.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Encourage students to highlight or note parts of the deliverables that feel most exciting or challenging. This helps you gauge engagement and plan support for different groups."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "66504a00-62bf-4b4f-85d5-95bc79d2ca71",
        "lesson_activity.key": "624a9385-01b9-40e0-8734-e85891423e60"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4c66af90-ad62-4521-aadb-b8efc78941d7",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct student to Level 1 to begin Milestone 1: Define Your Magazine. Students can use the tools on this level to support their work.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** As students work, ask guiding questions such as:\n- \"How would you describe your magazine's main audience in one sentence?\"\n- \"What kind of stories or visuals would fit your theme?\"\n- \"How might your design choices make your magazine feel more cohesive?\"\n\nUse these quick check-ins to confirm that students are connecting their creative choices to a clear audience and purpose.",
        "progression_name": "Milestone 1: Define Your Magazine",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Set expectations for pacing — Milestone 1 can typically be finished by the end of today's class or early next class. Encourage students to focus first on clarity of idea rather than polish; they'll refine visuals and layouts later in the project."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4c66af90-ad62-4521-aadb-b8efc78941d7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "624a9385-01b9-40e0-8734-e85891423e60"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f0cd5548-6d9f-4faf-9031-cda53f077caf",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f0cd5548-6d9f-4faf-9031-cda53f077caf",
        "lesson_activity.key": "624a9385-01b9-40e0-8734-e85891423e60"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "aa5b741e-8d35-4584-b7e0-b6665caac17c",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to complete the Milestone 1 Reflection section in their project planning guide. Explain that this reflection helps them capture what they learned today and how it will shape their next steps.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ensure students are discussing and sharing these reflection questions with a thought partner.",
        "duration": "5",
        "name": "Wrap Up",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If time permits, invite a few volunteers to share aloud or conduct a quick pair-and-share to close. Highlight that reflection is part of being an intentional designer — it helps them connect each day's work to their larger vision."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "aa5b741e-8d35-4584-b7e0-b6665caac17c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "624a9385-01b9-40e0-8734-e85891423e60"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "bcf3bbda-67d2-4457-a599-f4e62f107b60",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "bcf3bbda-67d2-4457-a599-f4e62f107b60",
        "lesson_activity.key": "624a9385-01b9-40e0-8734-e85891423e60"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "14ecb0e9-93eb-46cf-b4dc-c21aa91b24f4",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What's one element you're excited to see come to life from your design?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students reconnect with their design vision and build enthusiasm to begin the hands-on coding phase. This primes them to think intentionally about how their design ideas translate into real HTML/CSS builds today.",
        "duration": "5",
        "name": "Warm Up"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "14ecb0e9-93eb-46cf-b4dc-c21aa91b24f4",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e0619366-09df-4514-a718-7ccb016ab91e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2a3282db-bf20-45f0-8163-34d3475e65e3",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the tasks to complete for Day 2 of the project. Explain that today students will focus on Milestones 2 and 3. Direct students to open their Digital Magazine Project Guide and locate the Milestone 2 and 3 sections. Have them review the Goals and Deliverables for each milestone so they understand what to prioritize during work time.",
        "duration": "35",
        "name": "Activity",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Point out that these milestones move from building to refining. Encourage students not to aim for perfection at first—just to get their layout functioning, then improve it through feedback and iteration."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2a3282db-bf20-45f0-8163-34d3475e65e3",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e0619366-09df-4514-a718-7ccb016ab91e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "1b63afef-a769-4929-a5fb-97469c779ad4",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Levels 2 and 3 to work on their first draft of their pages. Clarify that they'll begin building the first draft of their magazine pages using HTML and CSS, with help from the AI tools available at these levels. Encourage students to use AI prompts strategically — for example, to generate layouts, apply color palettes, or organize text elements, while checking that the code makes sense.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ensure students are on task and progressing toward a complete first draft. Ask check-in questions like:\n- \"What part of your magazine are you starting with?\"\n- \"What feedback from your plan or Milestone 1 are you using as you build?\"\n- \"Have you tested your page to make sure it behaves the way you expect?\"\n\nProvide quick support if students get stuck — redirect them to the AI Chat or Project Support Bot for troubleshooting help before intervening directly.",
        "progression_name": "Milestone 2: Build Your First Draft"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "1b63afef-a769-4929-a5fb-97469c779ad4",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e0619366-09df-4514-a718-7ccb016ab91e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a5dc1596-c615-4e64-8b72-8788a51f420c",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Milestone 3: Refine and Align"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a5dc1596-c615-4e64-8b72-8788a51f420c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e0619366-09df-4514-a718-7ccb016ab91e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "1df73238-c344-4e4d-be5e-06b4c6d25a15",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain the TAG Peer Review process and model what thoughtful feedback looks like. Have students pair up or form small groups and TAG one to two peers' projects. They can leave feedback on sticky notes (digital or paper) directly at their peer's workspace or comment within the project guide if using shared docs. Emphasize that this is not a final critique — it's a chance to gather early insights before moving to Milestone 3.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Students may be at different points when it's time for peer review. Reassure them that work doesn't need to be complete to be reviewed — feedback during the process helps improve the final product.\nReinforce the mindset that design and development are iterative, and peer feedback offers new perspectives and guidance.\nIf time allows, invite a few students to share one piece of feedback they received that will guide their next steps."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "1df73238-c344-4e4d-be5e-06b4c6d25a15",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e0619366-09df-4514-a718-7ccb016ab91e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b9f67be7-4db8-493b-9c56-788b170d2c32",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b9f67be7-4db8-493b-9c56-788b170d2c32",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e0619366-09df-4514-a718-7ccb016ab91e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "41284b01-1efb-45c3-84b6-037ce66355ee",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to complete the Milestone 3 Reflection section in their project planning guide. Explain that this reflection helps them identify what's working well and what still needs adjustment before the final milestone. Give students a few minutes to reflect individually, then share with a partner or small group.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** As students write and discuss, listen for reflections that identify concrete next steps (e.g., \"I need to fix spacing,\" \"My navigation isn't consistent,\" or \"I want to make my site more accessible\"). Encourage students to connect these adjustments back to their user goals and audience experience.",
        "duration": "5",
        "name": "Wrap Up",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If time permits, invite a few students to share one key improvement they plan to make. Highlight that thoughtful reflection is a sign of growth—it shows they're thinking like real designers preparing to polish their final product."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "41284b01-1efb-45c3-84b6-037ce66355ee",
        "lesson_activity.key": "e0619366-09df-4514-a718-7ccb016ab91e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "cf63c10d-9912-49c6-8c21-8400c6c2bcc5",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What challenge do you still need to solve before your site is ready to share?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students identify one specific challenge or improvement area that will guide their focus during today's Milestone 4 – Test and Finalize work. This primes them to enter work time with clear direction and purpose.",
        "duration": "5",
        "name": "Warm Up"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "cf63c10d-9912-49c6-8c21-8400c6c2bcc5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32f1071b-210c-44a9-b555-948460802181"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d3c25f3f-fed7-4c91-ad2f-f0e9c042e602",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the tasks to complete for Day 3 of the project. Explain that today is focused on Milestone 4 – Test and Finalize, where students polish their site using feedback from peers, teachers, and their own self-assessment. Remind students to check their Digital Magazine Project Guide for the Milestone 4 deliverables, which include final usability, accessibility, and design checks.",
        "duration": "35",
        "name": "Activity",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Frame today as a celebration of their work and growth as designers. Say something like: \"Today's your chance to put the finishing touches on your magazine and share what you've built. Every project is unique — focus on making sure yours reflects your audience, your ideas, and your effort.\" If you're doing a showcase, preview how students will present (e.g., rotating stations, quick pitches, or feedback slips)."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d3c25f3f-fed7-4c91-ad2f-f0e9c042e602",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32f1071b-210c-44a9-b555-948460802181"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "233d3e60-ebe1-46f0-860a-6df64b79e63e",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "233d3e60-ebe1-46f0-860a-6df64b79e63e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32f1071b-210c-44a9-b555-948460802181"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "06a3e4b8-89ae-4bad-927c-ba9815015a95",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to the last two pages of their Digital Magazine Project Guide, where the project rubric is located. Have students review each category carefully and mark where they believe their project currently falls. Encourage honesty — the goal is to identify strengths and areas for continued growth as intentional designers.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Check that students are engaging thoughtfully with each rubric criterion, not rushing to completion.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students that self-assessment isn't just about scoring their project — it's a professional habit that helps them take ownership of their design choices. Say something like: \"Designers constantly evaluate their own work to make sure it aligns with their goals, audience, and purpose. This rubric helps you see where you've grown and what you can still refine.\"\nIf time allows, have students highlight one category they feel especially proud of and one they'd like to improve next time."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "06a3e4b8-89ae-4bad-927c-ba9815015a95",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32f1071b-210c-44a9-b555-948460802181"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "409d0236-af6e-4c03-aac5-f9c4abc91383",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Level 4 to finish developing their Digital Magazine projects. Explain that this is their final dedicated work session for Milestone 4 – Test and Finalize. Reinforce that today's goal is to prioritize improvements based on their self-assessment and TAG peer feedback, rather than trying to fix everything at once. Instruct students to use the feedback they received from their TAG review and self-assessment to finalize their Digital Magazine project. Have students submit their projects at the end of the allotted time.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ensure students are on task. Remind students to comment their code with meaningful descriptions. Have students review their rubric and prioritize work on any rows where they do not yet show extensive evidence.",
        "progression_name": "Milestone 4: Test and Finalize",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students that professional designers always prioritize fixes before a release. Say something like: \"You don't need to fix everything today — focus on what will have the biggest impact for your user. Iteration is about making smart choices with the time you have.\"\nIf time allows at the end, invite students to do a brief pair preview, where they open a peer's site and give one final piece of positive or constructive feedback."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "409d0236-af6e-4c03-aac5-f9c4abc91383",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32f1071b-210c-44a9-b555-948460802181"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b7967a22-e74c-46c7-902a-f4d2b946e6f5",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b7967a22-e74c-46c7-902a-f4d2b946e6f5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32f1071b-210c-44a9-b555-948460802181"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a15dbf52-5bb9-481e-9cdf-d5b20f6b5810",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Distribute several sticky notes to each student for the gallery walk.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students begin the Gallery Walk by displaying their digital magazines on their computers, then moving around the room to explore classmates' projects. As they visit each one, students should use their sticky notes to leave feedback, kudos, or questions following the TAG approach (Tell, Ask, Give). Encourage them to engage with a range of projects—not just those of close friends.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Move around the room to observe how students are engaging with the displayed projects. Encourage students to leave a note about what they find interesting or insightful about their peers' work. Ensure that students are thoughtfully engaging with a variety of projects, not just those of their closest peers.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Frame the Gallery Walk as a celebration of learning and creativity, not a critique. Say something like: \"This is your chance to see how everyone's ideas came to life in different ways. You might even get inspired by someone else's approach!\""
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a15dbf52-5bb9-481e-9cdf-d5b20f6b5810",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32f1071b-210c-44a9-b555-948460802181"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "faf58ffe-993d-4fa8-80cc-75332ca2e8f1",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "You've gone from planning and designing to building, testing, and refining. This reflection is your chance to capture how you've grown — not just as a coder or designer, but as someone who collaborates with AI intentionally.",
        "duration": "5",
        "name": "Wrap Up"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "faf58ffe-993d-4fa8-80cc-75332ca2e8f1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32f1071b-210c-44a9-b555-948460802181"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c8dacac9-8cbd-4e0e-b0ff-e04ba7576d60",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to complete the Final Reflection and Final Self-Check sections in their Digital Magazine Project Guide. Explain that this final step helps them consolidate their learning and ensure their site meets key design goals — usability, consistency, accessibility, and thoughtful use of AI.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Encourage students to elaborate on their answers with specific examples of how they used feedback or iteration to improve their project. If students finish early, prompt them to help peers finalize their submissions or review their rubric one more time for completeness.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "You can use the Digital Magazine Planning Guide as evidence for the Decomposition and Design Thinking and rubric criteria. The Final Reflection as evidence for Reflection and Iteration with AI rubric criteria."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c8dacac9-8cbd-4e0e-b0ff-e04ba7576d60",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32f1071b-210c-44a9-b555-948460802181"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c041b8c3-b791-41ac-bfad-9a0563ba67ec",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "name": "End of Lesson Survey",
        "progression_name": "End of Lesson Survey"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c041b8c3-b791-41ac-bfad-9a0563ba67ec",
        "lesson_activity.key": "32f1071b-210c-44a9-b555-948460802181"
      }
